From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Dmitry Afonchenko <undermove1@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 19 Nov 2026 22:02:51 +0400
Subject: [PATCH 187/202] Meridian: import from Google Chrome
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Arc's import now reads any Chromium browser (ImportSource: its profile
folders, its keychain item or Local State key, its profile ids). For Google
Chrome: a space per Chrome profile, named as in Chrome (Local State), its
bookmarks as pinned tabs and folders (the bar on top, Other and Mobile
bookmarks as folders), the tabs it had open (its last session file) as
Today tabs that load when opened; its other profiles in Meridian profiles
of their own; its sign-ins, passwords, cards, history, form entries,
addresses, site permissions, site searches and sites' data, as for Arc.
File > Import from Chrome…, and the welcome tour offers it when there is no
Arc. The mojo import methods take the source ("arc" or "chrome").

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01SwxrQ2eLfJ2bv8cCoG2va1
